    end_line: 529
    content: "---\nname: workspace-integration\ndescription: >-\n  Integrate 1P Google Workspace APIs (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Calendar, Gmail, Chat, Meet, Forms, Classroom, Tasks, Keep, People, Picker) into the application. Use when the user wants to authenticate with Google Workspace to read, write, or search Google Workspace data. Requires OAuth configuration via the set_up_oauth and remove_oauth tools.\n---\n\n# Google Workspace Integration\n\nThis skill guides you through integrating Google Workspace APIs into the\napplication. **Always start with OAuth configuration before writing any API\ncode.**\n\n## Step 1: Configure OAuth (MANDATORY)\n\nYou MUST configure OAuth before writing any code that uses Workspace APIs, or\nwhen modifying/updating an existing integration (adding or removing scopes):\n\n1.  **Determine desired scopes**:\n\n    *   Check if `scopes_to_add` is present in the metadata (passed in the chat\n        context). If present, these are the new scopes selected by the user to\n        add to the application. You MUST request these scopes and merge them\n        with any existing scopes in the codebase.\n    *   Check if `scopes_to_remove` is present in the metadata. If present,\n        these scopes MUST be removed.\n    *   If `scopes_to_add` is not present, determine the minimum scopes required\n        for the features you plan to implement.\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Least Privilege Principle (Scope Minimization)**:\n    >\n    > *   If `scopes_to_add` is present in the metadata (i.e., setup was\n    >     initiated from the integrations panel), you MUST request all new\n    >     scopes selected by the user.\n    > *   Otherwise (standard chat-driven flow), apply scope minimization:\n    >     *   Request only the minimum, most specific scopes required for the\n    >         requested feature. Do not request broad scopes if specific,\n    >         narrower scopes are sufficient.\n    >     *   If the user asks for integration with a specific Workspace File\n    >         type (such as Google Slides, Google Docs, Google Sheets, or Google\n    >         Forms), enable the API and add scopes for that file type only\n    >         (e.g., `documents.readonly`, `spreadsheets.readonly`,\n    >         `presentations.readonly`, or `forms.body`).\n    >     *   Add broad scopes like `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive` or\n    >         `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` only when the\n    >         user explicitly requests general Google Drive features (like\n    >         listing, searching, or managing non-specific files across Drive).\n\n2.  **Inspect current scopes**: Search the codebase (e.g., using `grep_search`\n    or `code_search` for `SCOPES` or `scopes`) to read the currently configured\n    scopes from the code.\n\n3.  **Identify changes**:\n\n    *   Compare current scopes in code with desired scopes.\n    *   Identify scopes to remove (present in code for the target Workspace\n        service, but NOT in desired scopes).\n    *   Identify scopes to add (present in desired scopes, but NOT in code).\n\n4.  **Remove scopes (if any)**: If there are scopes to remove:\n\n    > [!CAUTION]\n    >\n    > You MUST call the `remove_oauth` tool with the list of `scopes_to_remove`\n    > **BEFORE** you modify the codebase or delete any files.\n\n    *   Call the `remove_oauth` tool with the list of `scopes_to_remove`. (Note:\n        `remove_oauth` does not require user confirmation).\n    *   Remove these scopes from the codebase (either by updating the `SCOPES`\n        array or deleting the integration files entirely).\n\n        **Example: Updating the SCOPES array to remove Calendar events while\n        preserving Gmail**\n\n        ```diff\n         const SCOPES = [\n        -  \'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events\',\n           \'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly\',\n         ];\n        ```\n\n    *   Remove any features/code that depend on these removed scopes.\n\n5.  **Add scopes (if any)**: If there are scopes to add:\n\n    Merge the new scopes with existing ones in the codebase:\n\n    *   The combined list to use in the code and tool calls must be: (existing\n        scopes in code NOT belonging to target Workspace service) + (desired\n        scopes for target Workspace service).\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Simultaneous Addition and Removal**:\n    >\n    > If metadata contains BOTH `scopes_to_remove` AND (`scopes_to_add` or\n    > `requested_scopes`), you MUST perform BOTH tool calls in this turn: 1.\n    > Call `remove_oauth` with `scopes_to_remove`. 2. Call `set_up_oauth` with\n    > the target scopes and `userConfirmedInUI` set to `true` (if\n    > `user_confirmed_in_ui: true` is present in metadata) or `false` (if\n    > initiating setup).\n    >\n    > Do NOT omit calling `set_up_oauth` after calling `remove_oauth`!\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Project ID Precondition**:\n    >\n    > Treat any project ID extracted from `APP_URL` as an internal\n    > infrastructure project and ignore it. Only provide a `project_id` if the\n    > user has explicitly requested a specific Google Cloud project.\n\n    > [!NOTE]\n    >\n    > **Handling userConfirmedInUI**:\n    >\n    > *   If `user_confirmed_in_ui: true` is present in metadata (e.g., setup or\n    >     scope editing was initiated from the integrations panel), call\n    >     `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: true` and the combined scope\n    >     list.\n    > *   Otherwise (initiating setup from chat prompt):\n    >     *   If you have already called `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI:\n    >         false` in this conversation history for the required scopes,\n    >         proceed directly to **Step 7 (Critical Turn-2 Behavior)**.\n    >     *   Otherwise, call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false` and\n    >         the combined scope list, and pause for user confirmation.\n\n6.  **Pause for UI configuration (Turn-1)**:\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Yield execution** and wait for user confirmation immediately after\n    > calling `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`.\n\n    When you **STOP**, your text response MUST be specific about which Google\n    Workspace APIs are being enabled and what they will allow the app to do.\n    Follow these rules:\n\n    *   **Name the product(s)**: Use the full product name (e.g., \"Google\n        Calendar\", \"Gmail\", \"Google Drive and Google Sheets\").\n    *   **Describe the capability**: Explain what the integration enables in\n        plain language (e.g., \"see and update calendar events\", \"read and send\n        emails\", \"access and organize files\").\n    *   **Mention permission (MANDATORY)**: You MUST explicitly state that the\n        app will access or update data \"with permission\" or \"with permission\n        from the app\'s users\".\n    *   **Reference the card**: Say \"See the card below\" or \"Review the card\n        below\", NOT \"click the button\" or \"authorize the app\".\n    *   **Keep vocabulary non-technical**: Restrict message content to\n        functional capabilities and user-facing connection states. Omit\n        technical references to OAuth, scopes, or setup details.\n    *   **Connect to the user\'s goal**: Briefly tie it back to what the user\n        asked for.\n\n    Here are some examples of acceptable responses:\n\n    *   **Good example** (Calendar): \"See the card below to enable the Google\n        Calendar APIs for your app. Once you\'ve done that, I\'ll be able to add\n        features that can see and update your end users\' calendar events, with\n        permission from the app\'s users, and help you reclaim your time.\"\n\n    *   **Good example** (Drive + Sheets): \"Review the card below to connect\n        Google Drive and Google Sheets to your app. Once enabled, I\'ll add the\n        ability to browse files and read spreadsheet data to power your\n        dashboard.\"\n\n    *   **Bad example** \342\235\214: \"Please click the button in the OAuth setup UI to\n        authorize the app.\"\n\n7.  **Critical Turn-2 Behavior (Resuming)**: When you are resumed after the user\n    accepts/confirms:\n\n    *   Ensure the user has explicitly accepted the prompt (e.g., by saying \"I\n        agree\" or \"I accept, continue\").\n    *   Your VERY FIRST ACTION in that turn must be to call `set_up_oauth` with\n        `userConfirmedInUI: true` and the combined scope list.\n\n    > [!CAUTION]\n    >\n    > You MUST call the `set_up_oauth` tool again with `userConfirmedInUI: true`\n    > before performing any other task (such as writing integration code,\n    > modifying files, building, or linting). If you skip this tool call, the\n    > scopes will NOT be persisted for this applet, and the application will\n    > fail at runtime.\n\n8.  **Update codebase**: After finalizing configuration:\n\n    *   Update the codebase to include the new scopes in the `SCOPES` array and\n        implement the new features.\n\n9.  **Final Sync**: Ensure the codebase is fully updated and matches the final\n    desired set of scopes (or that all integration code is removed if\n    disabling):\n\n    *   Verify the changes compile and run successfully.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> Calling `set_up_oauth` will automatically provision Firebase Authentication\n> for sign-in. There is **no need** to call the `set_up_firebase` tool unless\n> you are also adding a Firestore database to the application.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> If the app already has OAuth configured with some scopes, you MUST preserve\n> those existing scopes. Read the current scope list from the code, add the new\n> scopes needed for the Workspace API, and pass the full combined list to\n> `set_up_oauth`.\n\n## Authentication & UI\n\nIf the application does not have a \"Sign in with Google\" button already, you\nMUST add one when integrating Workspace APIs.\n\n### 1. Client-Side Authentication (Firebase Auth)\n\nUse the **Firebase SDK** to authenticate and obtain an OAuth access token. The\nFirebase project is already provisioned for the applet \342\200\224 the config lives in\n`firebase-applet-config.json` at the project root.\n\nYou MUST style the sign-in button to resemble the official \"Sign in with Google\"\nbutton style. Here is an example of how to add the button:\n\n```html\n<button class=\"gsi-material-button\">\n  <div class=\"gsi-material-button-state\"></div>\n  <div class=\"gsi-material-button-content-wrapper\">\n    <div class=\"gsi-material-button-icon\">\n      <svg version=\"1.1\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 48 48\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" style=\"display: block;\">\n        <path fill=\"#EA4335\" d=\"M24 9.5c3.54 0 6.71 1.22 9.21 3.6l6.85-6.85C35.9 2.38 30.47 0 24 0 14.62 0 6.51 5.38 2.56 13.22l7.98 6.19C12.43 13.72 17.74 9.5 24 9.5z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#4285F4\" d=\"M46.98 24.55c0-1.57-.15-3.09-.38-4.55H24v9.02h12.94c-.58 2.96-2.26 5.48-4.78 7.18l7.73 6c4.51-4.18 7.09-10.36 7.09-17.65z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#FBBC05\" d=\"M10.53 28.59c-.48-1.45-.76-2.99-.76-4.59s.27-3.14.76-4.59l-7.98-6.19C.92 16.46 0 20.12 0 24c0 3.88.92 7.54 2.56 10.78l7.97-6.19z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#34A853\" d=\"M24 48c6.48 0 11.93-2.13 15.89-5.81l-7.73-6c-2.15 1.45-4.92 2.3-8.16 2.3-6.26 0-11.57-4.22-13.47-9.91l-7.98 6.19C6.51 42.62 14.62 48 24 48z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h48v48H0z\"></path>\n      </svg>\n    </div>\n    <span class=\"gsi-material-button-contents\">Sign in with Google</span>\n    <span style=\"display: none;\">Sign in with Google</span>\n  </div>\n</button>\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> You **MUST** implement in-memory caching for the access token. Do **NOT**\n> store the access token in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`. Use\n> `onAuthStateChanged` to clear the cached token when the user signs out.\n\nHere is an example of how to set up Firebase Auth and manage the access token in\nmemory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { initializeApp } from \'firebase/app\';\nimport { getAuth, signInWithPopup, GoogleAuthProvider, onAuthStateChanged, User } from \'firebase/auth\';\nimport firebaseConfig from \'../firebase-applet-config.json\';\n\nconst app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\nconst auth = getAuth(app);\n\nconst provider = new GoogleAuthProvider();\n// Request Workspace scopes\nprovider.addScope(\'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file\'); // Example: Drive scope\n// Add other Workspace scopes here as needed by the app\n\n// Flag to indicate if we are in the middle of a sign-in flow.\nlet isSigningIn = false;\n// Cache the access token in memory.\nlet cachedAccessToken: string | null = null;\n\n// Initialize auth state listener. Call this on app load.\nexport const initAuth = (\n  onAuthSuccess?: (user: User, token: string) => void,\n  onAuthFailure?: () => void\n) => {\n  return onAuthStateChanged(auth, async (user: User | null) => {\n    if (user) {\n      if (cachedAccessToken) {\n        if (onAuthSuccess) onAuthSuccess(user, cachedAccessToken);\n      } else if (!isSigningIn) {\n        cachedAccessToken = null;\n        if (onAuthFailure) onAuthFailure();\n      }\n    } else {\n      cachedAccessToken = null;\n      if (onAuthFailure) onAuthFailure();\n    }\n  });\n};\n\n// Must be called from a button click or user interaction\nexport const googleSignIn = async (): Promise<{ user: User; accessToken: string } | null> => {\n  try {\n    isSigningIn = true;\n    const result = await signInWithPopup(auth, provider);\n    const credential = GoogleAuthProvider.credentialFromResult(result);\n    if (!credential?.accessToken) {\n      throw new Error(\'Failed to get access token from Firebase Auth\');\n    }\n\n    cachedAccessToken = credential.accessToken;\n    return { user: result.user, accessToken: cachedAccessToken };\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    console.error(\'Sign in error:\', error);\n    throw error;\n  } finally {\n    isSigningIn = false;\n  }\n};\n\nexport const getAccessToken = async (): Promise<string | null> => {\n  return cachedAccessToken;\n};\n\nexport const logout = async () => {\n  await auth.signOut();\n  cachedAccessToken = null;\n};\n```\n\n### UI Handling and Auth State\n\nTo provide a good user experience, your application should show a login button\nwhenever the user is not authenticated or the token is unavailable.\n\n**Recommended Pattern:**\n\n1.  Use a state variable (e.g., `needsAuth`) to track if authentication is\n    required.\n2.  In a `useEffect` hook (or equivalent lifecycle method), call `initAuth` and\n    set `needsAuth` based on the result.\n3.  When making API calls, check if the token is available. If not, set\n    `needsAuth` to `true` to show the login button.\n\nExample React usage:\n\n```tsx\nconst [needsAuth, setNeedsAuth] = useState(false);\nconst [token, setToken] = useState<string | null>(null);\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\nconst [isLoggingIn, setIsLoggingIn] = useState(false);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  initAuth(\n    () => setNeedsAuth(false),\n    () => setNeedsAuth(true)\n  );\n}, []);\n\nconst handleLogin = async () => {\n  setIsLoggingIn(true);\n  try {\n    const result = await googleSignIn();\n    if (result) {\n      setToken(result.accessToken);\n      setUser(result.user);\n      setNeedsAuth(false);\n      // Reload data...\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(\'Login failed:\', err);\n  } finally {\n    setIsLoggingIn(false);\n  }\n};\n\n// Render login button if needsAuth is true\nif (needsAuth) {\n  return <button onClick={handleLogin}>Sign in with Google</button>;\n}\n```\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> If the applet already has Firebase initialized (e.g., for Firestore), do NOT\n> call `initializeApp` again. Reuse the existing `app` instance and add the\n> `GoogleAuthProvider` scope configuration alongside the existing auth setup.\n\n## User Confirmation for Destructive Operations (MANDATORY)\n\nWhen writing code that **updates, modifies, or deletes** end user data through\nany Workspace API, you **MUST** always include an explicit user confirmation\ndialog before the operation executes. This applies to any operation that mutates\nuser-owned data, including but not limited to:\n\n-   Deleting files, emails, events, documents, notes, or tasks\n-   Overwriting or updating existing file content, document text, or spreadsheet\n    data\n-   Sending emails or chat messages on behalf of the user\n-   Modifying calendar events, form responses, or contact information\n-   Moving files to trash or permanently removing data\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **NEVER** execute a destructive or mutating API call without first presenting\n> the user with a clear confirmation dialog that describes exactly what will be\n> changed or deleted. Silent data mutations are unacceptable.\n\n### Implementation Requirements\n\n1.  The confirmation dialog **MUST** clearly describe the action being taken\n    (e.g., \"Delete 3 files from Google Drive?\" or \"Update the contents of \'Q2\n    Report\'?\").\n2.  The dialog **MUST** require an explicit user action to proceed (e.g.,\n    clicking a \"Confirm\" or \"Delete\" button).\n3.  The dialog **SHOULD** offer a \"Cancel\" option that aborts the operation with\n    no side effects.\n4.  For bulk operations, the dialog **SHOULD** list the affected items or\n    indicate the count of items that will be affected.\n\n### Example: React Confirmation Dialog\n\n```tsx\nconst handleDeleteFiles = async (fileIds: string[]) => {\n  const confirmed = window.confirm(\n    `Are you sure you want to delete ${fileIds.length} file(s)? This action cannot be undone.`\n  );\n  if (!confirmed) return;\n\n  const accessToken = await getAccessToken();\n  for (const fileId of fileIds) {\n    await fetch(`https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files/${fileId}`, {\n      method: \'DELETE\',\n      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n    });\n  }\n};\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n>\n> For a better user experience, consider using a custom modal component instead\n> of `window.confirm()`, especially when you need to display detailed\n> information about the items being affected.\n\n## Supported APIs\n\nAPI       | Endpoint                   | Primary Scopes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Use Cases\n--------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------\nDrive     | `drive.googleapis.com`     | `drive`, `drive.activity`, `drive.activity.readonly`, `drive.appdata`, `drive.apps.readonly`, `drive.file`, `drive.install`, `drive.meet.readonly`, `drive.metadata`, `drive.metadata.readonly`, `drive.photos.readonly`, `drive.readonly`, `drive.scripts`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | File storage, browsing, upload/download\nCalendar  | `calendar.googleapis.com`  | `calendar`, `calendar.acls`, `calendar.acls.readonly`, `calendar.app.created`, `calendar.calendarlist`, `calendar.calendarlist.readonly`, `calendar.calendars`, `calendar.calendars.readonly`, `calendar.events`, `calendar.events.freebusy`, `calendar.events.owned`, `calendar.events.owned.readonly`, `calendar.events.public.readonly`, `calendar.events.readonly`, `calendar.freebusy`, `calendar.readonly`, `calendar.settings.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Event management, scheduling\nChat      | `chat.googleapis.com`      | `chat.admin.delete`, `chat.admin.memberships`, `chat.admin.memberships.readonly`, `chat.admin.spaces`, `chat.admin.spaces.readonly`, `chat.app.delete`, `chat.app.memberships`, `chat.app.memberships.readonly`, `chat.app.messages.readonly`, `chat.app.spaces`, `chat.app.spaces.create`, `chat.app.spaces.readonly`, `chat.customemojis`, `chat.customemojis.readonly`, `chat.delete`, `chat.import`, `chat.memberships`, `chat.memberships.app`, `chat.memberships.readonly`, `chat.messages`, `chat.messages.create`, `chat.messages.reactions`, `chat.messages.reactions.create`, `chat.messages.reactions.readonly`, `chat.messages.readonly`, `chat.spaces`, `chat.spaces.create`, `chat.spaces.readonly`, `chat.users.readstate`, `chat.users.readstate.readonly`, `chat.users.sections`, `chat.users.sections.readonly`, `chat.users.spacesettings` | Messaging, space management\nClassroom | `classroom.googleapis.com` | `classroom.addons.student`, `classroom.addons.teacher`, `classroom.announcements`, `classroom.announcements.readonly`, `classroom.courses`, `classroom.courses.readonly`, `classroom.coursework.me`, `classroom.coursework.me.readonly`, `classroom.coursework.students`, `classroom.coursework.students.readonly`, `classroom.courseworkmaterials`, `classroom.courseworkmaterials.readonly`, `classroom.guardianlinks.me.readonly`, `classroom.guardianlinks.students`, `classroom.guardianlinks.students.readonly`, `classroom.profile.emails`, `classroom.profile.photos`, `classroom.push-notifications`, `classroom.rosters`, `classroom.rosters.readonly`, `classroom.student-submissions.me.readonly`, `classroom.student-submissions.students.readonly`, `classroom.topics`, `classroom.topics.readonly`                                             | Course management, assignments\nDocs      | `docs.googleapis.com`      | `documents`, `documents.readonly`, `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Document reading and editing\nForms     | `forms.googleapis.com`     | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `forms.body`, `forms.body.readonly`, `forms.responses.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Form creation, response reading\nGmail     | `gmail.googleapis.com`     | `gmail.addons.current.action.compose`, `gmail.addons.current.message.action`, `gmail.addons.current.message.metadata`, `gmail.addons.current.message.readonly`, `gmail.compose`, `gmail.insert`, `gmail.labels`, `gmail.metadata`, `gmail.modify`, `gmail.readonly`, `gmail.send`, `gmail.settings.basic`, `gmail.settings.sharing`, `mail.google.com`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Email reading and sending\nKeep      | `keep.googleapis.com`      | `keep`, `keep.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Note management\nMeet      | `meet.googleapis.com`      | `meetings.space.created`, `meetings.space.readonly`, `meetings.space.settings`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Meeting management\nSheets    | `sheets.googleapis.com`    | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `spreadsheets`, `spreadsheets.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | Spreadsheet reading and editing\nSlides    | `slides.googleapis.com`    | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `presentations`, `presentations.readonly`, `spreadsheets`, `spreadsheets.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Presentation reading and editing\nTasks     | `tasks.googleapis.com`     | `tasks`, `tasks.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Task list management\nPeople    | `people.googleapis.com`    | `contacts`, `contacts.other.readonly`, `contacts.readonly`, `directory.readonly`, `user.addresses.read`, `user.birthday.read`, `user.emails.read`, `user.gender.read`, `user.organization.read`, `user.phonenumbers.read`, `userinfo.email`, `userinfo.profile`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | Contact and profile info\nPicker    | `picker.googleapis.com`    | `drive.file`, `drive.metadata.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Pick files from drive\n\nAll scopes are prefixed with `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/`.\n\n## API-Specific Guidance\n\nFor detailed scopes, concepts, and code patterns for each API, read the\ncorresponding reference file:\n\n-   `references/drive.md` \342\200\224 Google Drive\n-   `references/calendar.md` \342\200\224 Google Calendar\n-   `references/chat.md` \342\200\224 Google Chat\n-   `references/classroom.md` \342\200\224 Google Classroom\n-   `references/docs.md` \342\200\224 Google Docs\n-   `references/forms.md` \342\200\224 Google Forms\n-   `references/gmail.md` \342\200\224 Gmail\n-   `references/keep.md` \342\200\224 Google Keep\n-   `references/meet.md` \342\200\224 Google Meet\n-   `references/sheets.md` \342\200\224 Google Sheets\n-   `references/slides.md` \342\200\224 Google Slides\n-   `references/tasks.md` \342\200\224 Google Tasks\n-   `references/picker.md` \342\200\224 Google Picker\n-   `references/people.md` \342\200\224 People API\n-   `references/picker.md` \342\200\224 Picker API\n\n## Framework Patterns\n\n**Implement Client-Side Token Authentication**: Obtain OAuth tokens directly in\nthe client (browser) and pass them to backend routes via `Authorization: Bearer\n<token>` headers. Validate the incoming bearer token on the server.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n>\n> **No Server-Side OAuth Redirect Flows**: Do NOT use server-side OAuth code\n> flows (such as Express/Next.js redirect routes or `google.auth.OAuth2` with\n> redirect URIs). Preview environments run on dynamic, ephemeral URLs that\n> cannot be allowlisted in the GCP Console, causing `Error 400:\n> redirect_uri_mismatch` failures.\n\n### React (Client-Side Only)\n\nAll API calls happen in the browser using the access token from the OAuth flow:\n\n```typescript\nconst res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files\', {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\nconst data = await res.json();\n```\n\n### Next.js (Client-Side + Server-Side)\n\n**Client-side**: Same as React above.\n\n**Server-side** (API routes): Pass the access token from the client to your API\nroute, then call the Google API from the server:\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/drive/route.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \'next/server\';\n\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  if (!token) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \'Unauthorized\' }, { status: 401 });\n  }\n  const res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files\', {\n    headers: { Authorization: token },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n>\n> Prefer server-side API calls in Next.js when handling sensitive data or when\n> you need to transform/filter the response before sending it to the client.\n"
    raw_content: "---\nname: workspace-integration\ndescription: >-\n  Integrate 1P Google Workspace APIs (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Calendar, Gmail, Chat, Meet, Forms, Classroom, Tasks, Keep, People, Picker) into the application. Use when the user wants to authenticate with Google Workspace to read, write, or search Google Workspace data. Requires OAuth configuration via the set_up_oauth and remove_oauth tools.\n---\n\n# Google Workspace Integration\n\nThis skill guides you through integrating Google Workspace APIs into the\napplication. **Always start with OAuth configuration before writing any API\ncode.**\n\n## Step 1: Configure OAuth (MANDATORY)\n\nYou MUST configure OAuth before writing any code that uses Workspace APIs, or\nwhen modifying/updating an existing integration (adding or removing scopes):\n\n1.  **Determine desired scopes**:\n\n    *   Check if `scopes_to_add` is present in the metadata (passed in the chat\n        context). If present, these are the new scopes selected by the user to\n        add to the application. You MUST request these scopes and merge them\n        with any existing scopes in the codebase.\n    *   Check if `scopes_to_remove` is present in the metadata. If present,\n        these scopes MUST be removed.\n    *   If `scopes_to_add` is not present, determine the minimum scopes required\n        for the features you plan to implement.\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Least Privilege Principle (Scope Minimization)**:\n    >\n    > *   If `scopes_to_add` is present in the metadata (i.e., setup was\n    >     initiated from the integrations panel), you MUST request all new\n    >     scopes selected by the user.\n    > *   Otherwise (standard chat-driven flow), apply scope minimization:\n    >     *   Request only the minimum, most specific scopes required for the\n    >         requested feature. Do not request broad scopes if specific,\n    >         narrower scopes are sufficient.\n    >     *   If the user asks for integration with a specific Workspace File\n    >         type (such as Google Slides, Google Docs, Google Sheets, or Google\n    >         Forms), enable the API and add scopes for that file type only\n    >         (e.g., `documents.readonly`, `spreadsheets.readonly`,\n    >         `presentations.readonly`, or `forms.body`).\n    >     *   Add broad scopes like `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive` or\n    >         `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` only when the\n    >         user explicitly requests general Google Drive features (like\n    >         listing, searching, or managing non-specific files across Drive).\n\n2.  **Inspect current scopes**: Search the codebase (e.g., using `grep_search`\n    or `code_search` for `SCOPES` or `scopes`) to read the currently configured\n    scopes from the code.\n\n3.  **Identify changes**:\n\n    *   Compare current scopes in code with desired scopes.\n    *   Identify scopes to remove (present in code for the target Workspace\n        service, but NOT in desired scopes).\n    *   Identify scopes to add (present in desired scopes, but NOT in code).\n\n4.  **Remove scopes (if any)**: If there are scopes to remove:\n\n    > [!CAUTION]\n    >\n    > You MUST call the `remove_oauth` tool with the list of `scopes_to_remove`\n    > **BEFORE** you modify the codebase or delete any files.\n\n    *   Call the `remove_oauth` tool with the list of `scopes_to_remove`. (Note:\n        `remove_oauth` does not require user confirmation).\n    *   Remove these scopes from the codebase (either by updating the `SCOPES`\n        array or deleting the integration files entirely).\n\n        **Example: Updating the SCOPES array to remove Calendar events while\n        preserving Gmail**\n\n        ```diff\n         const SCOPES = [\n        -  \'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events\',\n           \'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly\',\n         ];\n        ```\n\n    *   Remove any features/code that depend on these removed scopes.\n\n5.  **Add scopes (if any)**: If there are scopes to add:\n\n    Merge the new scopes with existing ones in the codebase:\n\n    *   The combined list to use in the code and tool calls must be: (existing\n        scopes in code NOT belonging to target Workspace service) + (desired\n        scopes for target Workspace service).\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Simultaneous Addition and Removal**:\n    >\n    > If metadata contains BOTH `scopes_to_remove` AND (`scopes_to_add` or\n    > `requested_scopes`), you MUST perform BOTH tool calls in this turn: 1.\n    > Call `remove_oauth` with `scopes_to_remove`. 2. Call `set_up_oauth` with\n    > the target scopes and `userConfirmedInUI` set to `true` (if\n    > `user_confirmed_in_ui: true` is present in metadata) or `false` (if\n    > initiating setup).\n    >\n    > Do NOT omit calling `set_up_oauth` after calling `remove_oauth`!\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Project ID Precondition**:\n    >\n    > Treat any project ID extracted from `APP_URL` as an internal\n    > infrastructure project and ignore it. Only provide a `project_id` if the\n    > user has explicitly requested a specific Google Cloud project.\n\n    > [!NOTE]\n    >\n    > **Handling userConfirmedInUI**:\n    >\n    > *   If `user_confirmed_in_ui: true` is present in metadata (e.g., setup or\n    >     scope editing was initiated from the integrations panel), call\n    >     `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: true` and the combined scope\n    >     list.\n    > *   Otherwise (initiating setup from chat prompt):\n    >     *   If you have already called `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI:\n    >         false` in this conversation history for the required scopes,\n    >         proceed directly to **Step 7 (Critical Turn-2 Behavior)**.\n    >     *   Otherwise, call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false` and\n    >         the combined scope list, and pause for user confirmation.\n\n6.  **Pause for UI configuration (Turn-1)**:\n\n    > [!IMPORTANT]\n    >\n    > **Yield execution** and wait for user confirmation immediately after\n    > calling `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false`.\n\n    When you **STOP**, your text response MUST be specific about which Google\n    Workspace APIs are being enabled and what they will allow the app to do.\n    Follow these rules:\n\n    *   **Name the product(s)**: Use the full product name (e.g., \"Google\n        Calendar\", \"Gmail\", \"Google Drive and Google Sheets\").\n    *   **Describe the capability**: Explain what the integration enables in\n        plain language (e.g., \"see and update calendar events\", \"read and send\n        emails\", \"access and organize files\").\n    *   **Mention permission (MANDATORY)**: You MUST explicitly state that the\n        app will access or update data \"with permission\" or \"with permission\n        from the app\'s users\".\n    *   **Reference the card**: Say \"See the card below\" or \"Review the card\n        below\", NOT \"click the button\" or \"authorize the app\".\n    *   **Keep vocabulary non-technical**: Restrict message content to\n        functional capabilities and user-facing connection states. Omit\n        technical references to OAuth, scopes, or setup details.\n    *   **Connect to the user\'s goal**: Briefly tie it back to what the user\n        asked for.\n\n    Here are some examples of acceptable responses:\n\n    *   **Good example** (Calendar): \"See the card below to enable the Google\n        Calendar APIs for your app. Once you\'ve done that, I\'ll be able to add\n        features that can see and update your end users\' calendar events, with\n        permission from the app\'s users, and help you reclaim your time.\"\n\n    *   **Good example** (Drive + Sheets): \"Review the card below to connect\n        Google Drive and Google Sheets to your app. Once enabled, I\'ll add the\n        ability to browse files and read spreadsheet data to power your\n        dashboard.\"\n\n    *   **Bad example** \342\235\214: \"Please click the button in the OAuth setup UI to\n        authorize the app.\"\n\n7.  **Critical Turn-2 Behavior (Resuming)**: When you are resumed after the user\n    accepts/confirms:\n\n    *   Ensure the user has explicitly accepted the prompt (e.g., by saying \"I\n        agree\" or \"I accept, continue\").\n    *   Your VERY FIRST ACTION in that turn must be to call `set_up_oauth` with\n        `userConfirmedInUI: true` and the combined scope list.\n\n    > [!CAUTION]\n    >\n    > You MUST call the `set_up_oauth` tool again with `userConfirmedInUI: true`\n    > before performing any other task (such as writing integration code,\n    > modifying files, building, or linting). If you skip this tool call, the\n    > scopes will NOT be persisted for this applet, and the application will\n    > fail at runtime.\n\n8.  **Update codebase**: After finalizing configuration:\n\n    *   Update the codebase to include the new scopes in the `SCOPES` array and\n        implement the new features.\n\n9.  **Final Sync**: Ensure the codebase is fully updated and matches the final\n    desired set of scopes (or that all integration code is removed if\n    disabling):\n\n    *   Verify the changes compile and run successfully.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> Calling `set_up_oauth` will automatically provision Firebase Authentication\n> for sign-in. There is **no need** to call the `set_up_firebase` tool unless\n> you are also adding a Firestore database to the application.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> If the app already has OAuth configured with some scopes, you MUST preserve\n> those existing scopes. Read the current scope list from the code, add the new\n> scopes needed for the Workspace API, and pass the full combined list to\n> `set_up_oauth`.\n\n## Authentication & UI\n\nIf the application does not have a \"Sign in with Google\" button already, you\nMUST add one when integrating Workspace APIs.\n\n### 1. Client-Side Authentication (Firebase Auth)\n\nUse the **Firebase SDK** to authenticate and obtain an OAuth access token. The\nFirebase project is already provisioned for the applet \342\200\224 the config lives in\n`firebase-applet-config.json` at the project root.\n\nYou MUST style the sign-in button to resemble the official \"Sign in with Google\"\nbutton style. Here is an example of how to add the button:\n\n```html\n<button class=\"gsi-material-button\">\n  <div class=\"gsi-material-button-state\"></div>\n  <div class=\"gsi-material-button-content-wrapper\">\n    <div class=\"gsi-material-button-icon\">\n      <svg version=\"1.1\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 48 48\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" style=\"display: block;\">\n        <path fill=\"#EA4335\" d=\"M24 9.5c3.54 0 6.71 1.22 9.21 3.6l6.85-6.85C35.9 2.38 30.47 0 24 0 14.62 0 6.51 5.38 2.56 13.22l7.98 6.19C12.43 13.72 17.74 9.5 24 9.5z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#4285F4\" d=\"M46.98 24.55c0-1.57-.15-3.09-.38-4.55H24v9.02h12.94c-.58 2.96-2.26 5.48-4.78 7.18l7.73 6c4.51-4.18 7.09-10.36 7.09-17.65z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#FBBC05\" d=\"M10.53 28.59c-.48-1.45-.76-2.99-.76-4.59s.27-3.14.76-4.59l-7.98-6.19C.92 16.46 0 20.12 0 24c0 3.88.92 7.54 2.56 10.78l7.97-6.19z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"#34A853\" d=\"M24 48c6.48 0 11.93-2.13 15.89-5.81l-7.73-6c-2.15 1.45-4.92 2.3-8.16 2.3-6.26 0-11.57-4.22-13.47-9.91l-7.98 6.19C6.51 42.62 14.62 48 24 48z\"></path>\n        <path fill=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h48v48H0z\"></path>\n      </svg>\n    </div>\n    <span class=\"gsi-material-button-contents\">Sign in with Google</span>\n    <span style=\"display: none;\">Sign in with Google</span>\n  </div>\n</button>\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> You **MUST** implement in-memory caching for the access token. Do **NOT**\n> store the access token in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`. Use\n> `onAuthStateChanged` to clear the cached token when the user signs out.\n\nHere is an example of how to set up Firebase Auth and manage the access token in\nmemory:\n\n```typescript\nimport { initializeApp } from \'firebase/app\';\nimport { getAuth, signInWithPopup, GoogleAuthProvider, onAuthStateChanged, User } from \'firebase/auth\';\nimport firebaseConfig from \'../firebase-applet-config.json\';\n\nconst app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\nconst auth = getAuth(app);\n\nconst provider = new GoogleAuthProvider();\n// Request Workspace scopes\nprovider.addScope(\'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file\'); // Example: Drive scope\n// Add other Workspace scopes here as needed by the app\n\n// Flag to indicate if we are in the middle of a sign-in flow.\nlet isSigningIn = false;\n// Cache the access token in memory.\nlet cachedAccessToken: string | null = null;\n\n// Initialize auth state listener. Call this on app load.\nexport const initAuth = (\n  onAuthSuccess?: (user: User, token: string) => void,\n  onAuthFailure?: () => void\n) => {\n  return onAuthStateChanged(auth, async (user: User | null) => {\n    if (user) {\n      if (cachedAccessToken) {\n        if (onAuthSuccess) onAuthSuccess(user, cachedAccessToken);\n      } else if (!isSigningIn) {\n        cachedAccessToken = null;\n        if (onAuthFailure) onAuthFailure();\n      }\n    } else {\n      cachedAccessToken = null;\n      if (onAuthFailure) onAuthFailure();\n    }\n  });\n};\n\n// Must be called from a button click or user interaction\nexport const googleSignIn = async (): Promise<{ user: User; accessToken: string } | null> => {\n  try {\n    isSigningIn = true;\n    const result = await signInWithPopup(auth, provider);\n    const credential = GoogleAuthProvider.credentialFromResult(result);\n    if (!credential?.accessToken) {\n      throw new Error(\'Failed to get access token from Firebase Auth\');\n    }\n\n    cachedAccessToken = credential.accessToken;\n    return { user: result.user, accessToken: cachedAccessToken };\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    console.error(\'Sign in error:\', error);\n    throw error;\n  } finally {\n    isSigningIn = false;\n  }\n};\n\nexport const getAccessToken = async (): Promise<string | null> => {\n  return cachedAccessToken;\n};\n\nexport const logout = async () => {\n  await auth.signOut();\n  cachedAccessToken = null;\n};\n```\n\n### UI Handling and Auth State\n\nTo provide a good user experience, your application should show a login button\nwhenever the user is not authenticated or the token is unavailable.\n\n**Recommended Pattern:**\n\n1.  Use a state variable (e.g., `needsAuth`) to track if authentication is\n    required.\n2.  In a `useEffect` hook (or equivalent lifecycle method), call `initAuth` and\n    set `needsAuth` based on the result.\n3.  When making API calls, check if the token is available. If not, set\n    `needsAuth` to `true` to show the login button.\n\nExample React usage:\n\n```tsx\nconst [needsAuth, setNeedsAuth] = useState(false);\nconst [token, setToken] = useState<string | null>(null);\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\nconst [isLoggingIn, setIsLoggingIn] = useState(false);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  initAuth(\n    () => setNeedsAuth(false),\n    () => setNeedsAuth(true)\n  );\n}, []);\n\nconst handleLogin = async () => {\n  setIsLoggingIn(true);\n  try {\n    const result = await googleSignIn();\n    if (result) {\n      setToken(result.accessToken);\n      setUser(result.user);\n      setNeedsAuth(false);\n      // Reload data...\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(\'Login failed:\', err);\n  } finally {\n    setIsLoggingIn(false);\n  }\n};\n\n// Render login button if needsAuth is true\nif (needsAuth) {\n  return <button onClick={handleLogin}>Sign in with Google</button>;\n}\n```\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> If the applet already has Firebase initialized (e.g., for Firestore), do NOT\n> call `initializeApp` again. Reuse the existing `app` instance and add the\n> `GoogleAuthProvider` scope configuration alongside the existing auth setup.\n\n## User Confirmation for Destructive Operations (MANDATORY)\n\nWhen writing code that **updates, modifies, or deletes** end user data through\nany Workspace API, you **MUST** always include an explicit user confirmation\ndialog before the operation executes. This applies to any operation that mutates\nuser-owned data, including but not limited to:\n\n-   Deleting files, emails, events, documents, notes, or tasks\n-   Overwriting or updating existing file content, document text, or spreadsheet\n    data\n-   Sending emails or chat messages on behalf of the user\n-   Modifying calendar events, form responses, or contact information\n-   Moving files to trash or permanently removing data\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n>\n> **NEVER** execute a destructive or mutating API call without first presenting\n> the user with a clear confirmation dialog that describes exactly what will be\n> changed or deleted. Silent data mutations are unacceptable.\n\n### Implementation Requirements\n\n1.  The confirmation dialog **MUST** clearly describe the action being taken\n    (e.g., \"Delete 3 files from Google Drive?\" or \"Update the contents of \'Q2\n    Report\'?\").\n2.  The dialog **MUST** require an explicit user action to proceed (e.g.,\n    clicking a \"Confirm\" or \"Delete\" button).\n3.  The dialog **SHOULD** offer a \"Cancel\" option that aborts the operation with\n    no side effects.\n4.  For bulk operations, the dialog **SHOULD** list the affected items or\n    indicate the count of items that will be affected.\n\n### Example: React Confirmation Dialog\n\n```tsx\nconst handleDeleteFiles = async (fileIds: string[]) => {\n  const confirmed = window.confirm(\n    `Are you sure you want to delete ${fileIds.length} file(s)? This action cannot be undone.`\n  );\n  if (!confirmed) return;\n\n  const accessToken = await getAccessToken();\n  for (const fileId of fileIds) {\n    await fetch(`https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files/${fileId}`, {\n      method: \'DELETE\',\n      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n    });\n  }\n};\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n>\n> For a better user experience, consider using a custom modal component instead\n> of `window.confirm()`, especially when you need to display detailed\n> information about the items being affected.\n\n## Supported APIs\n\nAPI       | Endpoint                   | Primary Scopes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Use Cases\n--------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------\nDrive     | `drive.googleapis.com`     | `drive`, `drive.activity`, `drive.activity.readonly`, `drive.appdata`, `drive.apps.readonly`, `drive.file`, `drive.install`, `drive.meet.readonly`, `drive.metadata`, `drive.metadata.readonly`, `drive.photos.readonly`, `drive.readonly`, `drive.scripts`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | File storage, browsing, upload/download\nCalendar  | `calendar.googleapis.com`  | `calendar`, `calendar.acls`, `calendar.acls.readonly`, `calendar.app.created`, `calendar.calendarlist`, `calendar.calendarlist.readonly`, `calendar.calendars`, `calendar.calendars.readonly`, `calendar.events`, `calendar.events.freebusy`, `calendar.events.owned`, `calendar.events.owned.readonly`, `calendar.events.public.readonly`, `calendar.events.readonly`, `calendar.freebusy`, `calendar.readonly`, `calendar.settings.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Event management, scheduling\nChat      | `chat.googleapis.com`      | `chat.admin.delete`, `chat.admin.memberships`, `chat.admin.memberships.readonly`, `chat.admin.spaces`, `chat.admin.spaces.readonly`, `chat.app.delete`, `chat.app.memberships`, `chat.app.memberships.readonly`, `chat.app.messages.readonly`, `chat.app.spaces`, `chat.app.spaces.create`, `chat.app.spaces.readonly`, `chat.customemojis`, `chat.customemojis.readonly`, `chat.delete`, `chat.import`, `chat.memberships`, `chat.memberships.app`, `chat.memberships.readonly`, `chat.messages`, `chat.messages.create`, `chat.messages.reactions`, `chat.messages.reactions.create`, `chat.messages.reactions.readonly`, `chat.messages.readonly`, `chat.spaces`, `chat.spaces.create`, `chat.spaces.readonly`, `chat.users.readstate`, `chat.users.readstate.readonly`, `chat.users.sections`, `chat.users.sections.readonly`, `chat.users.spacesettings` | Messaging, space management\nClassroom | `classroom.googleapis.com` | `classroom.addons.student`, `classroom.addons.teacher`, `classroom.announcements`, `classroom.announcements.readonly`, `classroom.courses`, `classroom.courses.readonly`, `classroom.coursework.me`, `classroom.coursework.me.readonly`, `classroom.coursework.students`, `classroom.coursework.students.readonly`, `classroom.courseworkmaterials`, `classroom.courseworkmaterials.readonly`, `classroom.guardianlinks.me.readonly`, `classroom.guardianlinks.students`, `classroom.guardianlinks.students.readonly`, `classroom.profile.emails`, `classroom.profile.photos`, `classroom.push-notifications`, `classroom.rosters`, `classroom.rosters.readonly`, `classroom.student-submissions.me.readonly`, `classroom.student-submissions.students.readonly`, `classroom.topics`, `classroom.topics.readonly`                                             | Course management, assignments\nDocs      | `docs.googleapis.com`      | `documents`, `documents.readonly`, `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Document reading and editing\nForms     | `forms.googleapis.com`     | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `forms.body`, `forms.body.readonly`, `forms.responses.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Form creation, response reading\nGmail     | `gmail.googleapis.com`     | `gmail.addons.current.action.compose`, `gmail.addons.current.message.action`, `gmail.addons.current.message.metadata`, `gmail.addons.current.message.readonly`, `gmail.compose`, `gmail.insert`, `gmail.labels`, `gmail.metadata`, `gmail.modify`, `gmail.readonly`, `gmail.send`, `gmail.settings.basic`, `gmail.settings.sharing`, `mail.google.com`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Email reading and sending\nKeep      | `keep.googleapis.com`      | `keep`, `keep.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Note management\nMeet      | `meet.googleapis.com`      | `meetings.space.created`, `meetings.space.readonly`, `meetings.space.settings`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Meeting management\nSheets    | `sheets.googleapis.com`    | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `spreadsheets`, `spreadsheets.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | Spreadsheet reading and editing\nSlides    | `slides.googleapis.com`    | `drive`, `drive.file`, `drive.readonly`, `presentations`, `presentations.readonly`, `spreadsheets`, `spreadsheets.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Presentation reading and editing\nTasks     | `tasks.googleapis.com`     | `tasks`, `tasks.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Task list management\nPeople    | `people.googleapis.com`    | `contacts`, `contacts.other.readonly`, `contacts.readonly`, `directory.readonly`, `user.addresses.read`, `user.birthday.read`, `user.emails.read`, `user.gender.read`, `user.organization.read`, `user.phonenumbers.read`, `userinfo.email`, `userinfo.profile`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | Contact and profile info\nPicker    | `picker.googleapis.com`    | `drive.file`, `drive.metadata.readonly`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Pick files from drive\n\nAll scopes are prefixed with `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/`.\n\n## API-Specific Guidance\n\nFor detailed scopes, concepts, and code patterns for each API, read the\ncorresponding reference file:\n\n-   `references/drive.md` \342\200\224 Google Drive\n-   `references/calendar.md` \342\200\224 Google Calendar\n-   `references/chat.md` \342\200\224 Google Chat\n-   `references/classroom.md` \342\200\224 Google Classroom\n-   `references/docs.md` \342\200\224 Google Docs\n-   `references/forms.md` \342\200\224 Google Forms\n-   `references/gmail.md` \342\200\224 Gmail\n-   `references/keep.md` \342\200\224 Google Keep\n-   `references/meet.md` \342\200\224 Google Meet\n-   `references/sheets.md` \342\200\224 Google Sheets\n-   `references/slides.md` \342\200\224 Google Slides\n-   `references/tasks.md` \342\200\224 Google Tasks\n-   `references/picker.md` \342\200\224 Google Picker\n-   `references/people.md` \342\200\224 People API\n-   `references/picker.md` \342\200\224 Picker API\n\n## Framework Patterns\n\n**Implement Client-Side Token Authentication**: Obtain OAuth tokens directly in\nthe client (browser) and pass them to backend routes via `Authorization: Bearer\n<token>` headers. Validate the incoming bearer token on the server.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n>\n> **No Server-Side OAuth Redirect Flows**: Do NOT use server-side OAuth code\n> flows (such as Express/Next.js redirect routes or `google.auth.OAuth2` with\n> redirect URIs). Preview environments run on dynamic, ephemeral URLs that\n> cannot be allowlisted in the GCP Console, causing `Error 400:\n> redirect_uri_mismatch` failures.\n\n### React (Client-Side Only)\n\nAll API calls happen in the browser using the access token from the OAuth flow:\n\n```typescript\nconst res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files\', {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\nconst data = await res.json();\n```\n\n### Next.js (Client-Side + Server-Side)\n\n**Client-side**: Same as React above.\n\n**Server-side** (API routes): Pass the access token from the client to your API\nroute, then call the Google API from the server:\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/drive/route.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \'next/server\';\n\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  if (!token) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \'Unauthorized\' }, { status: 401 });\n  }\n  const res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files\', {\n    headers: { Authorization: token },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n>\n> Prefer server-side API calls in Next.js when handling sensitive data or when\n> you need to transform/filter the response before sending it to the client.\n"
    num_lines: 530
    num_bytes: 34612
  }
}
