  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m digging into the user\'s request, focusing on the core need: developing a web application. It seems the main function will involve managing both outgoing and incoming document records. My initial focus is on defining the specific features needed for this book-keeping system. I need to clarify the scope of the application and the type of information that will be stored.\n\n\n**Defining Specific Columns**\n\nI\'ve moved on to refining the details for the \"Outgoing Letter Registration Book\" specifically. I\'m focusing on defining the required columns, which are: \"\341\236\233.\341\236\232\", \"\341\236\201\341\237\222\341\236\233\341\236\271\341\236\230\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232\341\236\233\341\236\267\341\236\201\341\236\267\341\236\217 \341\236\220\341\237\222\341\236\204\341\237\203\341\236\221\341\236\270 \341\236\201\341\237\202 \341\236\206\341\237\222\341\236\223\341\236\266\341\237\206\", \"\341\236\205\341\237\206\341\236\223\341\236\275\341\236\223\", \"\341\236\200\341\237\222\341\236\232\341\236\237\341\236\275\341\236\204\341\236\221\341\236\221\341\236\275\341\236\233\", and \"\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\205\341\236\200\341\237\222\341\236\212\341\236\270\341\236\225\341\237\222\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\204\341\237\227\". I\'m making sure to adhere strictly to these five columns and ensuring no others are included. I\'m also confirming the header formatting and title as provided.\n\n\n**Defining Incoming Letter Details**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the \"Incoming Letter Registration Book,\" its structure, and associated information. I\'ve defined its title and header format, including \"\341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201....................... \341\236\212\341\236\233\341\237\213\341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201................... \341\236\237\341\236\232\341\236\273\341\236\224...................\" and the date range. I am also focusing on the five strict columns of \"\341\236\233.\341\236\232\", \"\341\236\201\341\237\222\341\236\233\341\236\271\341\236\230\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232\341\236\233\341\236\267\341\236\201\341\236\267\341\236\217 \341\236\200\341\237\222\341\236\232\341\236\237\341\236\275\341\236\204\341\236\212\341\236\276\341\236\230\", \"\341\236\205\341\237\206\341\236\223\341\236\275\341\236\223\", \"\341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201\341\236\233\341\236\267\341\236\201\341\236\267\341\236\217\341\236\212\341\236\276\341\236\230 \341\236\220\341\237\222\341\236\204\341\237\203\341\236\221\341\236\270 \341\236\201\341\237\202 \341\236\206\341\237\222\341\236\223\341\236\266\341\237\206\", and \"\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\205\341\236\200\341\237\222\341\236\212\341\236\270\341\236\225\341\237\222\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\204\341\237\227\". I\'ve got the data points clearly defined for the incoming letter management.\n\n\n**Structuring the Input Forms**\n\nI\'m now formulating data entry forms for both outgoing and incoming letters, ensuring they align perfectly with the defined columns. I\'ve designed fields for each column, including the auto-calculated/editable \"\341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201\341\236\232\341\237\200\341\236\204.\" The outgoing form covers content, date, quantity, receiving ministry, and remarks. The incoming form mirrors this but reflects the incoming letter details.\n\nI\'ve also begun to explore and create Google Sheets schemas for each. \"OutgoingLetters\" will have columns for ID, \341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201\341\236\232\341\237\200\341\236\204, \341\236\201\341\237\222\341\236\233\341\236\271\341\236\230\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232, date, quantity, receiving ministry, remarks and CreatedAt. And for the \"IncomingLetters\", I\'m including columns for ID, \341\236\233\341\237\201\341\236\201\341\236\232\341\237\200\341\236\204, \341\236\201\341\237\222\341\236\233\341\236\271\341\236\230\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232, originating ministry, quantity, and date.\n\n\n**Integrating Google Sheets**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the data storage strategy. The user\'s preference is Google Sheets, accessed via the Google Apps Script API. My plan includes an Apps Script generator and real-time syncing. We can also provide a direct Google Workspace OAuth option. The app will feature robust local persistence too.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data synchronization between the web application and Google Sheets. The user specified using the Google Apps Script API. I\'ve realized this is a superb, straightforward choice, and does not require workspace OAuth credentials for the schools and institutions that will be the target users. I am planning on generating Apps Script code for the user, alongside clear instructions for its setup and utilization. I will be sure to integrate a \"sync\" button for CSV and Google Sheets integration. I\'ll also explore offering Google Workspace OAuth or Google Sheets API if they prefer a different approach.\n\n\n\n**Revising OAuth Consideration**\n\nI am now carefully re-evaluating the OAuth configuration process. I realized the user wants to use the Google Apps Script API. My primary focus is to ensure the app functions without requiring Google Workspace OAuth credentials. I am re-assessing when to use the OAuth tools, specifically `set_up_oauth` and `remove_oauth`. I\'m going to only implement OAuth if the user specifically requests it.\n\n\n**Updating Metadata and HTML**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the application\'s initial setup, specifically the `metadata.json` and `index.html` files. I\'m updating `metadata.json` with the Khmer title and a descriptive summary. Then, I will update `index.html` to synchronize the title, description, and Open Graph meta tags with the `metadata.json` content, ensuring a clean initial configuration for the app.\n\n\n**Incorporating Khmer Fonts**\n\nI\'m now making sure the application supports Khmer fonts for official document presentation. I\'m focusing on integrating Google Fonts, specifically Khmer fonts like \'Kantumruy Pro\', \'Moul\', \'Siemreap\', and \'Battambang\', to ensure the correct look and feel. These fonts are essential for representing official Cambodian ministry letter books properly.\n\n\n\n**Designing Print Layout**\n\nI\'m now designing the print layouts for both incoming and outgoing letters. I\'m focusing on incorporating the date range and sequence number filters to dynamically generate the header and filter results. I\'ll need to allow users to select year, month, start/end sequence numbers, and start/end dates. I plan to use the date and sequence filters to dynamically generate the print titles.\n\n\n**Refining Print Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the printing feature and refining the UI for it. I am incorporating various paper sizes (A4 and A5, both landscape and portrait). I have added a print preview, with paper size switching and controls for margins and header visibility. The print CSS hides irrelevant elements to focus solely on the official book layout for clean printing.\n\n\n**Developing Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the application\'s user interface and feature set. I\'m focusing on the \"Add\", \"Edit\", and \"Delete\" operations, and also implementing real-time search functionality. I am creating a clean filter interface to provide data organization. I plan to incorporate printing and its preview. I will ensure comprehensive reporting through a dashboard.\n\n\n"
