  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve got the core dependencies, including `lucide-react`, `motion`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `react`, and `react-dom`. Now, I\'m evaluating if any additional packages are necessary. For exporting data to Excel or CSV, or for printing, I\'m leaning toward native CSV/Excel export functions, using styled, printable layouts with `window.print()` and custom print stylesheets. Let\'s see...\n\n\n**Assessing GAS Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Google Apps Script (GAS) integration requirements. The user\'s request details the database structure in Google Sheets, specifically `OutgoingLetters` and `IncomingLetters` sheets, and the need for a web application to interact with it via the GAS API. I need to design the best strategy for this.\n\n\n**Defining GAS Integration Strategy**\n\nI\'m solidifying the Google Apps Script (GAS) strategy. I\'ll provide complete GAS code in Settings with a copy button and Khmer instructions. The `doGet` function will fetch data as JSON, and `doPost` will manage actions like syncing and sheet initialization. Users will input the GAS Web App URL, test the connection, and auto-sync changes, with a manual option.\n\n\n**Implementing Offline Resilience**\n\nMy focus is now on ensuring offline functionality. I\'m prioritizing `localStorage` for all data to enable immediate use with sample letters, even before GAS configuration. I\'m also implementing a \"Sync with Google Sheets\" button with a timestamp and status. Export and import features for CSV, JSON, and Excel-compatible formats are also being integrated.\n\n**Refining Khmer Typography**\n\nI\'m solidifying the Khmer typography and layout. I\'ll load \'Kantumruy Pro\', \'Moul\', and \'Siemreap\' fonts. I will use \'Moul\' or a similar Khmer OS Muol Light style for official titles, and I\'ll add an official national motto header option to the print preview.\n\n\n**Calculating Book Headers**\n\nI\'m now calculating book headers dynamically. I will implement Khmer and English number toggling, and support dynamic calculations from the filtered dataset. I will offer overrides for year, month, number range, and date range. I\'ll need to calculate totals and date ranges in Khmer script. I will also have Khmer and English labels for date ranges.\n\n\n**Defining Book Content**\n\nI am now structuring the data fields for both incoming and outgoing letters in the books. I have included fields like serial number, summary, quantity, original letter details, remarks, and a dropdown for receiving ministries, ensuring a comprehensive and user-friendly system. I am expanding on the list of ministries.\n\n\n**Expanding Ministry List**\n\nI\'m expanding the list of receiving ministries to include \'Ministry of Civil Service\', \'Ministry of Health\', \'MFAIC\', \'MPTC\', \'Ministry of Environment\', \'MLVT\', \'Provincial/Capital DoEYS\', \'District Office\', \'Universities/HEIs\', and schools. Now the ministries are more organized.\n\n\n**Adding Institution Options**\n\nI\'m incorporating user-defined institution names alongside predefined options like Schools/High Schools and Development Partners. This ensures flexibility in the data entry process.\n\\n\\n\nI\'m now implementing the print features. I\'ll include support for A4 and A5 sizes, in both landscape and portrait orientations. I\'ll offer a print preview modal. I\'m prioritizing the official book cover page generation, including institution name, emblem, year, and letter number ranges. I also need to ensure clean page breaks and `@media print` styles for clean printing.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1078827"
