  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Font Customizations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on customizing fonts using Tailwind CSS v4. My goal is to add custom font utilities, specifically using `@theme` or font classes, and potentially `@media print` rules directly within `src/index.css`. I need to ensure these customizations are implemented correctly within the Tailwind framework, allowing for flexible font management.\n\n\n**Implementing Font Families**\n\nI\'ve integrated specific font families: \'Moul\', \'Siemreap\', \'Kantumruy Pro\', and \'Battambang\'. My default global font family is now \'Kantumruy Pro\', \'Siemreap\', sans-serif. I\'m also including `@media print` rules, which will allow for print-specific styling such as hiding elements with `.no-print`, showing elements with `.print-only`, and setting up exact print margins. I\'m also preparing print settings for A4 and A5 sizes.\n\n\n**Structuring Letter Data**\n\nI\'m currently structuring data for incoming letters, focusing on key attributes like summaries, dates, quantities, and recipient ministries. I\'m also incorporating system settings such as institution and department names, alongside the logo URL. I\'m aiming to define clear data models for efficient record-keeping and retrieval.\n\n\n**Defining System Settings**\n\nI\'m now integrating comprehensive system settings, including contact details, preferred paper sizes (A4 or A5), and orientation preferences (landscape or portrait). I\'m also addressing Google integration by incorporating Google Sheet IDs, Drive Folder IDs, and Script URLs for data synchronization. Finally, I\'m considering Khmer digit usage and the last synchronization timestamp, which is crucial for efficient data management.\n\n\n**Developing Data Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on generating realistic initial Cambodian education correspondence data, which will populate both outgoing and incoming letters in the application. I\'ve compiled a common ministries list. Additionally, I am working to define storage services, with functions for local storage management and Google Apps Script synchronization, and export and import features for CSV, Excel-compatible HTML and JSON data. I\'m also planning a template generator for Google Apps Script code.\n\n\n**Designing Top Bar Structure**\n\nI\'m presently outlining the top bar structure, dividing it into three zones: the brand title (\"\341\236\237\341\237\200\341\236\234\341\236\227\341\237\205\341\236\205\341\236\273\341\237\207\341\236\233\341\236\267\341\236\201\341\236\267\341\236\217\341\236\205\341\237\201\341\236\211-\341\236\205\341\236\274\341\236\233\"), navigation links (Dashboard, Outgoing Letters, Incoming Letters, Reports, Settings), and primary actions (Add Letter, Print, Sync). I\'m also planning the `DashboardView.tsx`, which will feature overview stats, recent entries, and sync status, and the `OutgoingLettersView.tsx`, which will contain a search/filter bar and register table.\n\n\n**Constructing Letter Views**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the implementation of both incoming and outgoing letter views. For the incoming letters, I\'m working on the book header calculation, search & filters bar, and a strict 5-column register table with actions for edit, delete and view functions. The forms for both incoming and outgoing letters are now being developed. Finally, I\'m working on the `PrintPreviewModal.tsx`, which will feature a dedicated print preview and correct aspect ratio.\n\n\n**Designing Book Printing**\n\nMy current focus is designing the precise print layout for official books. I\'m working on the book\'s header, which will dynamically display ranges of letter numbers and dates within the filtered data. I\'m also including options for a Cambodian motto and institution logo. The core structure is a five-column table with specific width ratios, borders, padding and font styling. I\'m also preparing a book cover generation tab. Finally, a `Print` button will trigger `window.print()`.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_522474"
      name: "edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Add Khmer fonts and print media styling in src/index.css\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\\n\\n@layer base {\\n  body {\\n    font-family: \'Kantumruy Pro\', \'Siemreap\', sans-serif;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n.font-moul {\\n  font-family: \'Moul\', \'Khmer OS Muol Light\', serif;\\n}\\n\\n.font-siemreap {\\n  font-family: \'Siemreap\', \'Khmer OS Siemreap\', sans-serif;\\n}\\n\\n.font-kantumruy {\\n  font-family: \'Kantumruy Pro\', sans-serif;\\n}\\n\\n.font-battambang {\\n  font-family: \'Battambang\', sans-serif;\\n}\\n\\n/* Print Specific Rules */\\n@media print {\\n  @page {\\n    margin: 12mm 10mm 12mm 10mm;\\n    size: auto;\\n  }\\n  \\n  body {\\n    background-color: white !important;\\n    color: black !important;\\n    font-size: 11pt !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  .no-print {\\n    display: none !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  .print-only {\\n    display: block !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  .printable-area {\\n    position: static !important;\\n    width: 100% !important;\\n    margin: 0 !important;\\n    padding: 0 !important;\\n    box-shadow: none !important;\\n    background: white !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  table {\\n    width: 100% !important;\\n    border-collapse: collapse !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  tr {\\n    page-break-inside: avoid !important;\\n  }\\n\\n  thead {\\n    display: table-header-group !important;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n@media screen {\\n  .print-only {\\n    display: none !important;\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"TargetContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\\n\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/index.css\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating index.css\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add Khmer fonts and print media CSS\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "edit_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 821389527
