  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Khmer Numerals**\n\nI\'m now focused on the utility file `src/utils/khmerNumerals.ts`. The primary task is crafting functions to convert Arabic numerals to Khmer numerals, with the mapping: 0 to \341\237\240, 1 to \341\237\241, and so on up to 9. I\'m also planning number formatting features like padding to ensure consistent output.\n\n\n**Expanding Khmer Functionality**\n\nI\'ve expanded beyond simple numeral conversion. Now, I\'m integrating Khmer month names into the system, enabling date formatting in Khmer: \"\341\236\220\341\237\222\341\236\204\341\237\203\341\236\221\341\236\270 \341\237\240\341\237\241 \341\236\201\341\237\202 \341\236\230\341\236\200\341\236\232\341\236\266 \341\236\206\341\237\222\341\236\223\341\236\266\341\237\206 \341\237\242\341\237\240\341\237\242\341\237\246\". I\'m also devising a calculation for book headers based on record arrays, incorporating logic for both empty and populated records. This includes finding the minimum and maximum numbers and dates for accurate header generation.\n\n\n"
