  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Document Uploads**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to handle document uploads, specifically for both outgoing and incoming communications. My current thinking is centered on integrating a system that allows for file attachments or links to external documents, streamlining the process of adding supporting materials. This functionality should be intuitive for diverse document types.\n\n\n**Implementing Document Uploads**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the document upload feature, placing the attachment functionality *after* the \"Remarks\" section in both outgoing and incoming letter forms. I plan to add fields in the data structure for file URLs, filenames, and file types to enable both uploads and external links. I\'m focusing on user experience, creating a clear section labeled \"\341\236\257\341\236\200\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232\341\236\227\341\237\222\341\236\207\341\236\266\341\236\224\341\237\213 (Attachment / Document)\" where users can select to upload a file or insert a link.\n\n\n**Refining File Handling**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the user interface for file management, allowing both file uploads via drag-and-drop or browsing, which will be encoded as data URLs, and external links like Google Drive. I\'m focusing on providing file details (name, size, preview) with clear controls. Critically, I must ensure the print layout maintains the mandated 5-column structure, potentially integrating attachment indicators within the \"Remarks\" column or a dedicated icon in the web view.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI for Attachments**\n\nI\'m now focusing intensely on the user interface, incorporating a sixth column, \"\341\236\257\341\236\200\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232\341\236\227\341\237\222\341\236\207\341\236\266\341\236\224\341\237\213,\" in the web view table for quick access and download, while ensuring a strict 5-column layout for print. This will use a toggle, if possible. The `LetterDetailModal` will display attachments with in-modal previews (PDF/Image) and a direct \"Open Attachment\" button. This layout is designed to maintain official standards in print.\n\n\n**Integrating File Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating file data. I\'m updating Google Sheets and the Apps Script template to include the \"AttachmentLink/AttachmentName\" column. I am updating `storageService.ts` to include `fileUrl` and `fileName` in sync payloads, exports, and imports. I\'m focusing on authentic UI design for both file uploads and URL links, with preview modals and clear icons. I need to add `attachmentUrl?` and `attachmentName?` to `OutgoingLetter` and `IncomingLetter` types in `index.ts`. I also must add the upload field to `OutgoingLetterModal.tsx` & `IncomingLetterModal.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Attachment Functionality**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface for the attachment section, placing it after \"\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\205\341\236\200\341\237\222\341\236\212\341\236\270\341\236\225\341\237\222\341\236\237\341\237\201\341\236\204\341\237\227.\" I\'ll implement a toggle for either file upload (reading the file and storing the name and data URL, including size limits) or URL entry, supporting various link types. Existing attachments will display with view/delete options. The web tables will integrate an \"\341\236\257\341\236\200\341\236\237\341\236\266\341\236\232\341\236\227\341\237\222\341\236\207\341\236\266\341\236\224\341\237\213\" column with quick preview capabilities. I\'ll maintain clean print format.\n\n\n"
